Subject: [PATCH 0014] pymalloc under Sublet: every block issued and revoked by the allocator
Upstream: CPython 3.13.7
Upstream-Archive: https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.7/Python-3.13.7.tgz
Upstream-SHA256: 6c9d80839cfa20024f34d9a6dd31ae2a9cd97ff5e980e969209746037a5153b2
Build-Variants: capstone64 domain (musl), Sublet arm
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1
Replaces: cpython-3.13.7-0009-pymalloc-arena-pointer.patch -- APPLY THIS INSTEAD
          OF 0009, never both

0009 keeps the pointer the arena allocator returned (arena_ptr, read through
_Py_ARENA_PTR) and derives every pool from it. The Sublet adapter refuses
exactly that: pym_arena_alloc returns an opaque token, "not an alias spanning
the arena's children", because an arena-wide alias still reaches a revoked
block's memory and per-block revocation would mean nothing. So inside obmalloc
the two are mutually exclusive, and this patch carries the other half of 0009's
job -- provenance -- in the adapter's vocabulary:

- pool_address is an address again (uintptr_t), and every pool and block pointer
  is handed out by pym_pool_create / pym_block_pointer: address in, freshly
  derived capability out. The two asserts that 0002 had rewritten as pointer
  comparisons go back to their upstream integer form.
- pym_issue at every hand-out (mrev + delin), pym_release at every free
  (revoke), pym_resize on a successful realloc including an in-place one, and
  pym_requested so a moved realloc copies only the old requested length.
- the >512-byte fallback goes to the adapter's separately accounted raw
  allocator, which has the same lifetime hooks.

Because the set applies this patch INSTEAD of 0009, it also carries whatever
of 0009 the Sublet arm still needs:

- 0009's pymacro.h and _PyMem_FreeDelayed/_PyObject_FreeDelayed hunks,
  verbatim. They do not conflict, and the plain arm keeps them in 0009, so
  the two copies must stay identical. The alignment builtins still matter
  here although POOL_ADDR no longer uses them: stringlib's fastsearch
  dereferences _Py_ALIGN_DOWN's result, and without them it reads through
  an address.
- the two statistics walks, _PyInterpreterState_GetAllocatedBlocks and
  _PyObject_DebugMallocStats, take each pool's header from pym_pool_pointer,
  where 0009 derives it from arena_ptr.

An earlier revision said 0009 kept all of this. It could not: 0009 is
skipped whole. Every interpreter exit then faulted in the first walk, at
shutdown (cause 24 in _PyInterpreterState_FinalizeAllocatedBlocks on an
integer pool address, 2026-09-25, interpreter corpus cases 4 7 13 17 18).

The transitions are the ones the component port's block-lifetime patch
identified (ports/cpython/pymalloc/patches/*-0003-*): ten of its twelve hunks
apply here unchanged, and the two that do not are the pool_address sites the
interpreter's own 0002 had already rewritten.

